{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-42138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-42138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa5d1118320cd4760df9123fb8eab1232e75eb8781a11436d856259f68736a6a"} {"question" "q-42138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-42138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-42138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & y & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & z & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 10 \\\\ 2 & y & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & z\\end{aligned}|=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & y & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & z & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & y & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & z & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 10 \\\\ 2 & y & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & z\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa5d1118320cd4760df9123fb8eab1232e75eb8781a11436d856259f68736a6a"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & m & b & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & n & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}m & b \\\\ 0 & n\\end{aligned}|=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a block lower triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & m & b & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & n & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & m & b & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & n & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}m & b \\\\ 0 & n\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-6)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa5d1118320cd4760df9123fb8eab1232e75eb8781a11436d856259f68736a6a"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-42"] ["math" "-50"] ["math" "-72"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "60"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-109271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-72"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa5d1118320cd4760df9123fb8eab1232e75eb8781a11436d856259f68736a6a"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that \n$|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3t\\end{aligned}|=\\frac{3}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3t\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/state.json" "file_sha256" "68150c2d14b8c9c70e3e012c9939a274a08b7cc777330792edb3c897c0c5919e"} {"question" "q-131654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053675/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa5d1118320cd4760df9123fb8eab1232e75eb8781a11436